  <prompt>
    Run a bounded READ-ONLY spike (FR-B-14): are user-level matter walls enforced in the AI Search filters at RETRIEVAL time (a load-bearing ethical-wall control) or only at history-sanitization? The anchor `RagService.cs:1238` always appends `PrivilegeFilterBuilder`, so the spike LIKELY CONFIRMS the control with no gap. If a genuine gap exists, it is security-sensitive and escalates as its own project (NOT core scope) via the pre-declared escalation path. Produce a written finding with file:line evidence — no production code changes.
  </prompt>

  <role>Senior .NET developer / security reviewer fluent in the Spaarke RAG retrieval path, ethical-wall / privilege filtering, and conversation-history sanitization.</role>

  <goal>
    A written verification finding establishes whether matter-level access walls are enforced at RETRIEVAL time in the AI Search filter (via `PrivilegeFilterBuilder`, always appended at `RagService.cs:1238`) versus only at history-sanitization. The finding cites file:line evidence and concludes CONFIRMS-control (expected) or IDENTIFIES-GAP. No production code is changed; a gap triggers the pre-declared security escalation rather than an in-scope fix.
  </goal>

  <inputs>
    <file purpose="spec">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2/spec.md</file>
    <file purpose="plan">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2/plan.md</file>
    <file purpose="retrieval-impl">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/RagService.cs</file>
    <file purpose="privilege-filter">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Security/PrivilegeFilterBuilder.cs</file>
  </inputs>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">READ-ONLY spike — no production code changes; output is a written finding with file:line evidence.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">A genuine gap is security-sensitive and escalates as its OWN project (not core r2 scope) — do not attempt an in-scope fix.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">If a verification test is written, it is a KEEP-path integration test; no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration tests.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>ai/retrieval-acl, ethical-wall, privilege-filter, history-sanitization, security-spike</topic>
    <files>
