    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Retrieval-time privilege filter (verify here)" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/RagService.cs:1238">PrivilegeFilterBuilder always appended to the AI Search filter at retrieval — the load-bearing control the spike confirms.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Privilege filter builder" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Security/PrivilegeFilterBuilder.cs">The filter construction — verify it encodes user-level matter walls.</pattern>
      <pattern name="History sanitization (the alternative site)" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Safety/CrossMatter/ConversationHistorySanitizer.cs">History-sanitization path — confirm walls are enforced at RETRIEVAL, not only here.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <context>
    <background>R22 asks whether ethical walls hold at retrieval or only at history-sanitization. Plan §3 notes retrieval ACL is "already enforced" (RagService.cs:1238 always appends PrivilegeFilterBuilder) so the spike LIKELY CONFIRMS. The escalation path is pre-declared because if the wall were only at sanitization, that would be a real ethical-wall gap warranting its own security project.</background>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="n/a">Independent read-only spike.</dependency>
