  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A written finding states whether matter walls are enforced at RETRIEVAL time (PrivilegeFilterBuilder at RagService.cs:1238) with file:line evidence.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The finding contrasts retrieval-time vs history-sanitization enforcement and concludes CONFIRMS-control or IDENTIFIES-GAP.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No production code is changed (read-only spike).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: if a gap is found, it is escalated as a separate security project — the spike does NOT attempt an in-scope fix (documented in the finding).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the spike finds matter walls are enforced ONLY at history-sanitization and NOT at retrieval (a real ethical-wall gap), STOP — this is security-sensitive (CLAUDE.md §6). Invoke the pre-declared escalation: file it as its own security project with the evidence; do not remediate within core r2 scope.</trigger>
  </escalation>
</task>
